questions.answer:
(a) One suitable program:

forever:
    moisture = read_analog(P0)
    if moisture < 30:
        pump = 1
    elif moisture > 60:
        pump = 0
    if moisture > 90:
        buzzer = 1
    else:
        buzzer = 0

(b) The two thresholds create hysteresis. If the pump switched on and off around a single value, small changes or sensor noise could make it start and stop repeatedly. The soil also takes time to absorb water. With these thresholds, the pump stays on until the soil has become properly wet (above 60), then stays off until it has dried out (below 30). This protects the pump and gives more stable watering.
